SDR Oxide (sdroxide) is a native software-defined-radio transceiver
client written in Rust.  It provides a PowerSDR/Thetis-style desktop
interface, browser-served remote operation, CAT/TCI/HPSDR and multiple
native SDR backends, including SoapySDR, RTL-SDR, HackRF, Airspy,
RX-888, SDRplay, LimeSDR and others.

The upstream project also includes digital-mode DSP, CW/RTTY/PSK
skimmers, FT8/FT4, FreeDV/RADE, logbook and built-in TCI and Hamlib
rigctld servers.
